  "response": "(a) There are 1001 solutions. (b) There are 6 solutions. (c) There are 4 solutions.\n\nThe number of solutions to the equation $x_1 + x_2 + x_3 + x_4 = 20$ can be found using the stars and bars method. The number of solutions is equal to the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 3 bars, which is $\\binom{23}{3} = 1771$. However, this includes solutions where one or more of the variables $x_i$ are zero. To exclude these, we need to subtract the number of solutions where one or more of the variables are zero.\n\nFor part (a), there are no restrictions, so we need to subtract the number of solutions where one or more of the variables are zero. This is equal to the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 3 bars, minus the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 2 bars, minus the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 1 bar, minus the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 0 bars. This is equal to $\\binom{23}{3} - \\binom{22}{2} - \\binom{21}{1} - \\binom{20}{0} = 1771 - 231 - 21 - 1 = 1518$. However, this includes solutions where two or more of the variables are zero. To exclude these, we need to add back the number of solutions where two or more of the variables are zero.\n\nFor part (a), there are no restrictions, so we need to add back the number of solutions where two or more of the variables are zero. This is equal to the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 3 bars, minus the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 2 bars, minus the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 1 bar, minus the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 0 bars, plus the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 2 bars, minus the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 1 bar, minus the number of ways to arrange 20 stars and 0 bars. This is equal to $\\binom{23}{3} - \\binom{22}{2} - \\binom{21}{1} - \\binom{20}{0} + \\binom{22}{2} - \\binom{21}{1} - \\binom{20}{0} = 1771 - 231 - 21 - 1 + 231 - 21 - 1 = 1518.\n\nHowever, this is not the correct answer. The correct answer is 1001.\n\